@startuml
title User Registration - /api/v1/auth/register POST (AllowAnonymous)

start

:Controller receives Register request;

note right
Input Field:
- FullName
- Email
- MobileNumber
- Password
- DesignationId
- GenderId
end note

:Send RegisterCommand to MediatR;

:Validate command data;

if (Validation failed?) then (Yes)

    :Return 400 Bad Request - Validation failed;
    stop

endif

:RegisterHandler executes;

:Begin transaction;

:Check if Email already exist;

if (Email exist?) then (Yes)

    :Return 409 Conflict - Email already exist;
    stop

endif

:Map DTO to Person entity;

note right
Person Entity Mapping:
- FullName -> FullName
- Email -> Email
- MobileNumber -> MobileNumber
- DesignationId -> DesignationId
- GenderId -> GenderId
end note

:Call Auth Service to add Person;

:Create User entity linked to Person;

:Call Auth Service to add User;

:Hash password and create UserSecret;

note right
UserSecret Entity Mapping:
- UserId -> UserId
- hash -> PasswordHash
- salt -> PasswordSalt
end note

:Call Auth Service to add UserSecret;

:Assign default STUDENT role to User;

:Call Auth Service to add UserRoleMapping;

:Call Auth Service to SaveChanges;

:Get role name for the User;

:Call JWT Helper to generate Access and Refresh token;

:Create RefreshToken entity;

note right
RefreshToken Entity Mapping:
- UserId -> UserId
- response.RefreshToken -> Token
- DateTime.UtcNow + ExpiryDays -> ExpiryDate
- false -> IsRevoked
end note

:Call Auth Service to add RefreshToken;

:Call Auth Service to SaveChanges;

:Commit transaction;

:Return 200 OK - Authentication token;

stop

@enduml
